  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HNGLA-Access to Children rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Hong Ngu City Lawyers&#x2019; Association has identified the recent concerning issues regarding school violence, sexual abuse and injuries in children and came up with the initiative in responding to such problems limited to within 2 communes of Binh Thanh and Tan Hoi in Hong Ngu city, Dong Thap province. The objective of this initiative is to raise awareness for children and people about Children&apos;s Rights and Cybersecurity Law. Specifically, through a series of communication activities designed for students at Binh Thanh Primary School, Binh Thanh Secondary School, Tan Hoi Primary School, and Tan Hoi Secondary School, the children, teacher and parents will be able to access to and improve legal knowledge on Children&apos;s Rights and Cybersecurity Law. Through creative communication means (talk show, clubs,..), the project expects to create influence and impact on related stakeholders regarding their responsibility and ability to speak up about the mentioned issues. In particular, the project highly promotes the participation of students in models and clubs to enforce and promote the acknowledgment and practice of Children&apos;s Rights and Cybersecurity Law at 4 schools. Moreover, the Association also aims to provide legal advice for people and children within the project area on Children&apos;s Rights, Law on Cybersecurity and issues related to child protection, care and education, contributing to reducing violence against school violence, sexual abuse and injuries in children. The estimated result of the initiative includes: raising awareness for 800 parents and 1200 students, providing legal advice to 400 people and students on Children&apos;s Rights, Law on Cybersecurity and gender &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; sexuality issues related, targeting 400 students and 400 parents will sign a commitment to comply with the provisions on ensuring the Children&apos;s Rights and the Cybersecurity Law.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Union</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hong Ngu City Lawyers&#x2019; Association is a socio-political organization-profession working for the purpose of defending justice, equality, and social development; protecting the legitimate rights and interests and democratic freedoms of the citizens; protecting the independence and sovereignty of the territory and the directives and policies of the Party and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam righteously and unanimously. The association was newly established in 2019, yet the participating lawyers of the Association have had many years of experiences in the activities of legal aid and legal knowledge propagation. Annually, the Hong Ngu City Lawyers&#x2019; Association cooperates with the Department of Justice of Dong Thap province and the Governmental Legal Aid Center of Dong Thap province todeploy legal support activities and disseminate legal knowledge to people in the city and surrounding districts. Especially, the Association and the project staff have cooperated with An Giang University to implement projects in the 1st and 3rd Call of Justice Initiatives Facilitation Funds (JIFF) &#x2013; Oxfam. Additionally, the Association will continue to utilize their experiences to enhance collaboration with partners and related governmental agencies, building a cooperative network among all stakeholders to maximize the benefit and effectiveness of their activities, particularly in legal aid and legal communication.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lawyers Association of Hong Ngu cit</narrative>
  </participating-org>
